UID:camargo-fellowship-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261102T092458Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: Camargo Fellowship 2027-2028 for Artists\, Scholars and T
 hinkers (Cassis\, France)
DESCRIPTION:The Camargo Foundation invites artists\, scholars and thinkers 
 to its flagship Core Fellowship: a ten-week self-directed residency on its
  clifftop campus overlooking the Mediterranean in Cassis\, France\, dedica
 ted to research\, experimentation and interdisciplinary exchange. Curators
  apply under the Thinkers category\, which covers accomplished professiona
 ls and practitioners in cultural and creative fields who are professionall
 y engaged in critical thought\, including curators\, critics and journalis
 ts\; projects should engage theoretical\, artistic or societal questions. 
 WHAT YOU GET: a stipend of EUR 350 per week (EUR 3\,500 total)\, basic tra
 nsportation funding\, and a furnished apartment with an equipped kitchen o
 n campus. Fourteen fellowships are awarded per year: seven for artists and
  seven for scholars and thinkers. RESIDENCY PERIODS: Fall 2027 (8 Septembe
 r to 17 November 2027) or Spring 2028 (23 February to 4 May 2028). ELIGIBI
 LITY: artists in visual arts\, performance\, writing\, film\, music or mul
 tidisciplinary work with at least 5 years of professional practice\; schol
 ars holding or pursuing a PhD focused on French and Francophone cultures o
 r cross-cultural Mediterranean studies\; and thinkers as described above. 
 APPLICATION: via Submittable with a 100-word proposal summary\, a 1\,200-w
 ord proposal narrative\, a 300-word rationale for Camargo\, a 300-word car
 eer-stage rationale\, a CV (max 3 pages)\, work samples and two references
 . NOTE: the foundation has announced that this is the final Fellowship sel
 ected through a public open call until further notice\; a new selection pr
 ocess begins in July 2027\, making this the last chance to apply directly.
 \n\nOrganisation: Camargo Foundation\nLocation: Camargo Foundation campus\
 , Cassis\, France. Open worldwide.\nAward: EUR 350 per week (EUR 3\,500 to
 tal for the ten-week residency)\, plus basic travel funding and a furnishe
 d apartment with equipped kitchen on the Camargo campus. 14 fellowships pe
 r year: 7 for artists and 7 for scholars and thinkers. No application fee.
 \nDuration: Ten weeks\, either 8 September to 17 November 2027 or 23 Febru
 ary to 4 May 2028.\n\nMore: https://camargofoundation.org/en/camargo-fello
 wship-2026-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://camargofoundation.org/en/camargo-fellowship-2026-2027?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Camargo Foundation campus\, Cassis\, France. Open worldwide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:culture360-asef-arts-in-the-wake-of-ai-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261102T092458Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260929
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260930
SUMMARY:Deadline: culture360 / ASEF: Call for Content\, Arts in the Wake of
  AI
DESCRIPTION:culture360.ASEF.org\, the arts platform of the Asia-Europe Foun
 dation\, invites proposals from writers and content producers for its open
  call 'Arts in the Wake of AI': articles\, podcasts and video interviews t
 hat foreground how cultural professionals and organisations across Asia an
 d Europe are adapting to AI technologies\, from generative tools and machi
 ne learning to recommender systems and algorithms. WHAT THEY WANT: case-st
 udy-based contributions grounded in real-world evidence\, experiences or p
 ractices\, on topics including the impact of AI on cultural diversity\, fa
 irness and inclusivity\; the environmental costs of AI in the cultural sec
 tor\; and AI governance in the cultural sector (policy\, copyright\, intel
 lectual property and the ethical use of AI-generated cultural content). Ac
 ademic research papers and non-arts subjects are not considered. FEE: SGD 
 250 per commissioned article\, podcast or video interview. FORMATS: journa
 listic articles of 800 to 1\,000 words with at least four credited images\
 ; podcasts and video interviews of 15 to 20 minutes. ELIGIBILITY: national
 s of ASEM partner countries with previous experience in writing\, podcasti
 ng or video production\, proficiency in English\, and knowledge of or invo
 lvement in the Asian and European arts and culture scene\; an existing cha
 nnel for further dissemination is an advantage\; the work is fully virtual
 . Up to two proposals per application. Only selected writers are notified.
  Queries to culture[at]asef.org. Deadline 29 September 2026 at 6 PM Singap
 ore time\, via the online application form.\n\nOrganisation: Asia-Europe F
 oundation (ASEF)\, culture360.ASEF.org\nLocation: Fully remote\; contribut
 ors do not need to be based in Singapore. Open to nationals of ASEM partne
 r countries across Asia and Europe.\nAward: SGD 250 fee per commissioned a
 rticle\, podcast or video interview. Up to two proposals per application\,
  of which at most one is selected. No application fee.\nDuration: One-off 
 editorial commissions: articles of 800 to 1\,000 words with at least four 
 credited pictures\, podcasts and video interviews of 15 to 20 minutes\n\nM
 ore: https://culture360.asef.org/opportunities/call-for-content-arts-ai/?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://culture360.asef.org/opportunities/call-for-content-arts-ai/?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Fully remote\; contributors do not need to be based in Singapore. 
 Open to nationals of ASEM partner countries across Asia and Europe.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:american-academy-berlin-prize-2027-28@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261102T092458Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260926
SUMMARY:Deadline: American Academy in Berlin: Berlin Prize Fellowship 2027-
 28
DESCRIPTION:The American Academy in Berlin is an independent\, nonprofit in
 stitute for advanced study in the arts\, humanities\, social sciences\, la
 w\, journalism and public policy\, whose primary mission is to strengthen 
 the cultural and intellectual ties between the United States and Germany. 
 Each year\, after a rigorous selection process\, the Academy awards roughl
 y two dozen semester-long Berlin Prize fellowships to individuals who demo
 nstrate excellence in their fields. DISCIPLINES: applications are welcome 
 across the humanities\, social sciences\, law\, journalism and various are
 as of public policy. The Academy generally encourages projects addressing 
 pressing issues of the day\, specifically naming democracy\, security\, te
 chnology and society (especially AI)\, energy including climate\, and glob
 al order. Dedicated fellowships also support projects in Jewish studies\, 
 German studies\, and public health and biotechnology. Project proposals ne
 ed not focus on Germany\, but candidates should explain how a residency in
  Berlin would enhance their work. NOT ACCEPTED: proposals in mathematics o
 r the natural sciences. NOTE FOR ARTISTS: visual artists and composers are
  invited through separate\, nomination-based competitions\, so there is no
  open application route for them here. ELIGIBILITY: fellowships are restri
 cted to citizens and permanent residents of the United States. Both emergi
 ng and established figures are eligible. PhD holders qualify as emerging s
 cholars with a strong record of peer-reviewed work beyond the dissertation
 \; candidates in non-academic fields such as journalism\, filmmaking and p
 olicy need a significant record of publication or production\; fiction and
  nonfiction writers must have published at least one book with a reputable
  press. WHAT FELLOWS DO: fellows present their work to audiences in and ar
 ound Berlin through lectures\, readings\, public discussions\, performance
 s and film screenings\, and should be willing to engage with relevant Germ
 an institutions\, organizations and the media\; these activities are integ
 ral to the Academy's mission of fostering transatlantic dialogue. APPLICAT
 ION MATERIALS: a project proposal of 1\,500 to 1\,750 words plus a one-pag
 e bibliography\; a curriculum vitae of up to 10 pages\; two writing sample
 s totalling no more than 60 pages\; and three letters of recommendation\, 
 which are due 2 October 2026. DEADLINE: Friday 25 September 2026 at 12:00 
 noon Eastern Time (18:00 Central European Time). TIMELINE: all candidates 
 are notified of the competition outcome by email in late March 2027\; the 
 2027-28 Berlin Prize recipients are announced in May 2027.\n\nOrganisation
 : American Academy in Berlin\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany\, at the Hans Arn
 hold Center. RESTRICTED: fellowships are open only to citizens and permane
 nt residents of the United States.\nAward: Monthly stipend of USD 5\,000\,
  plus roundtrip airfare\, accommodation at or near the Hans Arnhold Center
 \, partial board\, in-house library services and professional networking o
 pportunities. Roughly two dozen fellowships awarded each year. No applicat
 ion fee.\nDuration: One full academic semester (about 4 months). Fall runs
  mid-August to mid-December\; spring runs late January to late May.\n\nMor
 e: https://www.americanacademy.de/apply/apply-for-a-fellowship/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.americanacademy.de/apply/apply-for-a-fellowship/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany\, at the Hans Arnhold Center. RESTRICTED: fellows
 hips are open only to citizens and permanent residents of the United State
 s.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fondsbjp-dossiersubsidie-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261102T092458Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fonds BJP: Dossiersubsidie for Freelance Regional and Loc
 al Journalists (autumn 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:The Dossiersubsidie is the Fonds BJP scheme for freelance regio
 nal and local journalists in the Netherlands who want to follow one subjec
 t properly rather than chase daily news\, funding up to EUR 19\,200 for si
 x months of sustained reporting on a single dossier. It is aimed at the ga
 p left by shrinking regional newsrooms\, where structural coverage of loca
 l government\, housing\, care or industry rarely gets paid time. ELIGIBILI
 TY: freelance journalists working in Dutch regional and local media only (
 staff journalists and national-only reporters are directed to the fund's o
 ther schemes). The fund also runs a year-round Vooronderzoekssubsidie of u
 p to EUR 8\,800 for preliminary research and a year-round Uitvoeringssubsi
 die of up to EUR 38\,600 for carrying out projects\, both open to all jour
 nalists. APPLICATION WINDOW: 17 August to 14 September 2026\, via the Fond
 s BJP subsidy portal. Online office hours on 8 September 2026\; questions 
 on 020 63 86 295.\n\nOrganisation: Fonds Bijzondere Journalistieke Project
 en (Fonds BJP)\nLocation: Netherlands\; for freelance journalists working 
 on Dutch regional and local reporting\nAward: Up to EUR 19\,200 for six mo
 nths of work on a single reporting dossier. No application fee.\nDuration:
  Six months of dedicated reporting on one subject area\n\nMore: https://ww
 w.fondsbjp.nl/subsidies/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
URL:https://www.fondsbjp.nl/subsidies/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands\; for freelance journalists working on Dutch regional 
 and local reporting
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:les-antipodes-numeric-2026-the-word@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261102T092458Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260908
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260909
SUMMARY:Deadline: Numeric 2026: The Word (Les antipodes Research and Creati
 on Residency)
DESCRIPTION:Two research and creation residency grants in Agullana\, Catalo
 nia\, for artists\, thinkers and scientists of any branch (formal\, natura
 l\, social\, applied) working at the intersection of art\, culture\, scien
 ce and thought. THIS YEAR'S THEME\, The Word\, is squarely about large lan
 guage models. The framework moves from the word as creative principle acro
 ss traditions (the Judeo-Christian creating God\, the Quran as uncreated w
 ord\, the Sanskrit Om and the Vedas\, mantras that summon rather than desc
 ribe) to science relocating that intuition in the cell (Sagan's four-lette
 r alphabet of DNA as a material text\, Margulis countering that the langua
 ge of life is chemistry\, Witzany holding that all cell interactions are s
 ign-mediated)\, and then to LLMs\, which for the first time detach the wor
 d from the flesh and generate text through a probabilistic architecture tr
 ained on human language. The call asks what LLMs reveal about authorship\,
  originality and meaning when a system generates text that moves\, persuad
 es or deceives without experience or intention\, and whether we can still 
 say the models operate exclusively on human experience once they ingest th
 eir own output. It explicitly wants work that blurs comprehension and simu
 lation\, authorship and recombination\, and it names antecedents worth kno
 wing before applying: Ramon Llull's Ars Magna\, Joan Brossa's Sextina cibe
 rnetica\, Oulipo constraint writing\, oracles and divination\, oral-formul
 aic transmission\, translation as probabilistic approximation\, exquisite 
 corpses\, Burroughs's cut-ups\, automatic writing\, musical improvisation 
 and scientific simulation. Les antipodes asks for engagement 'beyond the i
 nstrumental use of the tools' and away from utopian and dystopian framings
 . WHAT YOU GET: spacious\, luminous\, independent work spaces plus a share
 d terrace in the centre of the village\, spaces for meeting\, dialogue and
  public presentation\, introductions to local\, academic\, artistic and pr
 ofessional contacts on request\, and support organising any activities tha
 t arise. The residency ends with an informal presentation\, and results ma
 y feed into the publications or public programme of Les antipodes. IMPORTA
 NTLY\, this is not an acquisition prize and involves no transfer of rights
 : authorship and intellectual property stay with the creators\, and select
 ion implies no acquisition of the work. Credits on resulting work must ack
 nowledge Numeric 2026 and its collaborators. WHO CAN APPLY: open to everyo
 ne of legal age\, any discipline or origin\, individually or as a collecti
 ve\, with the stipend shared among collective members. Applications must b
 e in Catalan or English whatever the working language of the project\, sub
 mitted through the online form with an optional PDF of up to 5 pages and 1
 0 MB. One application per person or collective. EVALUATION\, in order of w
 eight: singularity and innovation\; relevance to this year's LLM framework
 \; and interaction and transfer of value\, meaning relations with the soci
 al and geographical environment of Agullana and the Emporda and a plan for
  presenting the outcome in editorial\, on-site\, performative\, sound\, au
 diovisual or other form. The call may be declared void if no proposal reac
 hes the required level. PRACTICAL: residents must hold their own health co
 ver (EHIC for EU citizens\, or valid travel or health insurance for Spain 
 otherwise) and are responsible for their own equipment. Supported by the G
 eneralitat de Catalunya\, Agullana and Figueres town councils\, and Accion
  Cultural Espanola through the PICE national residencies programme. Terms 
 are published in Arabic\, Catalan\, English\, Spanish\, French and Chinese
 .\n\nOrganisation: Les antipodes\, with Bolit Centre d'Art Contemporani Gi
 rona and Museu de l'Emporda Figueres\nLocation: Agullana\, Alt Emporda\, C
 atalonia\, Spain. A village of 900 people\, 20 km from Figueres and the Vi
 lafant high-speed rail station\, 40 km from Perpignan\, 60 km from Girona\
 , 160 km from Barcelona.\nAward: Two grants. Each provides a stipend of EU
 R 1\,000 as taxable base (taxes and withholdings apply)\, round-trip trave
 l within the European Union\, and accommodation and meals for the four wee
 ks in Agullana. Travel and meals cover the resident only\, though the shar
 ed apartment can host immediate family by arrangement. Numeric also provid
 es the resources specified in the application and agreed during preparatio
 n. No application fee. Note that if a selected candidate lacks the profess
 ional registration needed to receive the stipend and payment has to be arr
 anged through Les antipodes\, the resulting costs are deducted from the st
 ipend.\nDuration: Four weeks\, 2 to 30 November 2026\, with both residenci
 es running simultaneously. Preceded by one month of preparation and follow
 ed by a two-month closing period. Applications 23 July to 8 September 2026
 \; decision announced 22 September 2026.\n\nMore: https://lesantipodes.com
 /numeric/2026_bases_en.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
URL:https://lesantipodes.com/numeric/2026_bases_en.html?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Agullana\, Alt Emporda\, Catalonia\, Spain. A village of 900 peopl
 e\, 20 km from Figueres and the Vilafant high-speed rail station\, 40 km f
 rom Perpignan\, 60 km from Girona\, 160 km from Barcelona.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kunstfonds-publikation-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261102T092458Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270116
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stiftung Kunstfonds: KUNSTFONDS_Publikation 2027 (up to E
 UR 24\,000)
DESCRIPTION:Grant for a single artist publication\, analog or digital forma
 ts included\, by freelance visual artists or artist duos\; media artists a
 re eligible. The call opened 1 October 2026. FUNDING: up to EUR 24\,000 pe
 r project with at least 10% own contribution (third-party funds allowed). 
 ELIGIBILITY: primary residence in Germany\; not enrolled as a student\; ar
 tists may apply to only one KUNSTFONDS programme per year. NOTE: the sibli
 ng KUNSTFONDS_Stipendium (EUR 18\,000 for 6 months) is expected to open mi
 d-December 2026 with the same deadline. DEADLINE: 15 January 2027\, 24:00.
 \n\nOrganisation: Stiftung Kunstfonds\nLocation: Bonn\, Germany (foundatio
 n). RESTRICTED: freelance visual artists or duos with primary residence in
  Germany\; enrolled students excluded.\nAward: Up to EUR 24\,000 per publi
 cation project\; a minimum 10% own contribution is required and may come f
 rom third parties. No application fee.\nDuration: Per project\n\nMore: htt
 ps://www.kunstfonds.de/foerderung/kunstfonds-publikation/bewerbung-und-ver
 gabe?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.kunstfonds.de/foerderung/kunstfonds-publikation/bewerbung-u
 nd-vergabe?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Bonn\, Germany (foundation). RESTRICTED: freelance visual artists 
 or duos with primary residence in Germany\; enrolled students excluded.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:daad-artists-in-berlin-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261102T092458Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261216
SUMMARY:Deadline: DAAD Artists-in-Berlin Program 2028 (Berliner Kuenstlerpr
 ogramm: literature\, music and sound\, film)
DESCRIPTION:One of the best-known international artist residencies: establi
 shed artists live and work in Berlin for a year (six months for film) and 
 become part of the city's cultural scene. Applications are open in literat
 ure\, music and sound\, and film\; visual arts fellows are nominated by a 
 jury and cannot apply. ELIGIBILITY: established artists with their own voi
 ce and standing\, no upper age limit\; students and recent graduates are n
 ot eligible (doctoral students are). German nationals and artists residing
  primarily in Germany are excluded\, with narrow exceptions for German dua
 l nationals abroad and recent arrivals. Alumni cannot reapply. Window open
 ed 19 October 2026\; deadline 15 December 2026\, 23:59 CET.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: DAAD Artists-in-Berlin Program (Berliner Kuenstlerprogramm)\nLocation: 
 Berlin\, Germany. In person.\nAward: Monthly stipend to cover living expen
 ses and rent (amount not published)\, furnished apartment\, and economy tr
 avel and luggage costs (also for partners and children living in Berlin fo
 r the full fellowship). No application fee.\nDuration: 12 months for liter
 ature and music and sound\; 6 months for film.\n\nMore: https://www.berlin
 er-kuenstlerprogramm.de/en/application/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.berliner-kuenstlerprogramm.de/en/application/?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany. In person.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:extra-residence-livre-objet-fabrique-pola-2027@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20261102T092458Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261109
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261110
SUMMARY:Deadline: EXTRA Residency 2027: Book-Object on Architecture\, Publi
 shing and Pedagogy (EUR 6\,000 bursary\, Fabrique POLA\, Bordeaux)
DESCRIPTION:EXTRA\, a Bordeaux association that publishes book-objects abou
 t space\, invites proposals for a residency to create a book-object at the
  crossroads of architecture\, publishing and pedagogy\, hosted at Fabrique
  POLA in Bordeaux. Residents spend four weeks of research and creation bet
 ween January and June 2027 and test the project with a public of their cho
 osing (for example early childhood\, school groups or older people). WHO: 
 artists\, architects\, landscape architects\, urban planners\, graphic des
 igners\, authors and other professionals interested in questions of space\
 ; individual\, duo or collective applications\; no age limit and no stated
  geographic restriction\, though the call is in French. The project must b
 e unpublished and not already under a publishing contract\, and applicants
  must be able to step away from other work during the residency periods. W
 HAT YOU GET: a EUR 6\,000 bursary in three instalments (one bursary per pr
 oject\, even for collectives)\, up to EUR 500 for materials and up to EUR 
 1\,000 for travel on receipts (sustainable transport preferred)\, accommod
 ation for up to two people\, a workspace at Fabrique POLA\, support from E
 XTRA for the research and public experiments\, a presentation at the venue
 \, and possible publication of the book-object under a separate contract w
 ith EXTRA. APPLICATION: free\; see the call page for conditions\, criteria
  and application guidance\, or contact extra.editeurdespaces@gmail.com. DE
 ADLINE: 9 November 2026.\n\nOrganisation: EXTRA (Editeur d'espaces)\, host
 ed at Fabrique POLA\nLocation: Fabrique POLA\, Bordeaux\, France. No geogr
 aphic restriction stated\; the call is published in French.\nAward: EUR 6\
 ,000 bursary (paid in three instalments\; not multiplied for duos or colle
 ctives)\, up to EUR 500 for materials and up to EUR 1\,000 for travel on r
 eceipts\, accommodation covered. No application fee.\nDuration: 4 weeks of
  research and creation between January and June 2027.\n\nMore: https://www
 .alternatif-art.com/appel-a-candidature/residence-extra-2027-livre-objet-a
 rchitecture-et-pedagogie/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
URL:https://www.alternatif-art.com/appel-a-candidature/residence-extra-2027
 -livre-objet-architecture-et-pedagogie/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Fabrique POLA\, Bordeaux\, France. No geographic restriction state
 d\; the call is published in French.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
